================================================================================
Third-party material
================================================================================

The Wizard's Brush was written after reading and comparing multiple upstream projects.
What was taken from each, and under which terms, is recorded here rather than
left to be inferred from a comment. Every item below is also attributed at its
use site.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reused under permissive licences
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SD.Next: https://github.com/vladmandic/automatic
    Copyright the SD.Next authors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    backend/app/modelprobe.py contains tensor-name markers that identify a
    checkpoint's family, adapted from SD.Next's `modules/model_probe.py`. Those
    markers were verified by that
    project against real checkpoints, which is the part that is hard to redo.

InvokeAI: https://github.com/invoke-ai/InvokeAI
    Copyright the InvokeAI authors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    backend/app/generators/vram.py follows the design of InvokeAI's
    `backend/util/vae_working_memory.py`: predicting VAE decode cost from output
    area so tiling becomes a decision rather than an unconditional default.

SwarmUI: https://github.com/mcmonkeyprojects/SwarmUI
    Copyright (c) 2024-2025 Alex "mcmonkey" Goodwin. Licensed under the MIT License.

    backend/app/params.py adapts the `ParamsQueried` idea: recording which
    parameters a handler actually read, so saved metadata cannot claim a setting
    took effect when it did not. backend/app/notify.py follows the design of
    SwarmUI's WebhookManager.

Uncensored-Local-Studio: https://github.com/techjarves/Uncensored-Local-Studio
    Licensed under the MIT License.

    The backend diagnosis and capability surfaces follow its useful lifecycle
    principle: an unavailable engine remains visible with a reason, and a model
    artifact is not called ready merely because a directory exists. The code,
    API shape, and React implementation in The Wizard's Brush are independent.

open-generative-ai: https://github.com/Anil-matcha/Open-Generative-AI
    Licensed under the MIT License.

    The schema-driven form audit informed restore-time value coercion and
    dependent option/range narrowing. The Wizard's Brush uses its own registry shape,
    renderer, validation, and tests; no catalogue data or source was copied.

HiDream-O1-Image: https://github.com/HiDream-ai/HiDream-O1-Image
    Copyright (c) 2026 HiDream.ai. Licensed under the MIT License.

    `remote_gpu.py` fetches the publisher's official runner at a pinned commit
    into the operator's remote runtime when the optional HiDream model is
    enabled. The upstream runner is not bundled in this repository. Wizards
    Brush invokes its documented interface and changes the documented optional
    attention flag for portability; it carries no upstream source expression.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Read and reimplemented; NOT copied
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The projects below are GPL-3.0 or AGPL-3.0. The Wizard's Brush is Apache-2.0, so no
code from them may be incorporated. Where the better idea was on their side it was
reimplemented from the observable behaviour or the wire format, never from their
source. These entries exist so that boundary is auditable rather than asserted.

ComfyUI: https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI (GPL-3.0)
    backend/app/wsframe.py carries previews as binary WebSocket frames. The
    convention of a big-endian uint32 type prefix is a wire format, not
    copyrightable expression; the framing here adds a job id, a tolerant decoder
    for unknown types, and shares no code with ComfyUI's `BinaryEventTypes`.

    Latent-to-RGB preview matrices: ComfyUI ships constants for these. None were
    copied. backend/app/generators/latent_rgb.py ships an EMPTY table, populated
    only by scripts/fit_preview_matrix.py, which derives a projection from the
    model itself with a least-squares solve.

krita-ai-diffusion: https://github.com/Acly/krita-ai-diffusion (GPL-3.0)
    backend/app/errors.py classifies failures into numeric severity bands so that
    ">= warning" is a threshold test. The banding idiom is the same one HTTP
    status codes use; the members, the values in use, and the implementation are
    our own.

Fooocus: https://github.com/lllyasviel/Fooocus (GPL-3.0)
    Its simple-versus-advanced product design and mask-focused inpaint behavior
    were studied. The Wizard's Brush independently implements a registry-driven
    Simple/Full form, source-space mask geometry, and its own metadata reader.
    No Fooocus source, constants, or specially licensed inpaint material was copied.

AUTOMATIC1111 stable-diffusion-webui:
https://github.com/AUTOMATIC1111/stable-diffusion-webui (AGPL-3.0)
    Its persisted parameter conventions, grid behavior, mask handling, and
    adapter UX were studied as ecosystem behavior. The Wizard's Brush independently
    implements its own routers, parameter versioning, geometry, and UI. The
    A1111 parameters block is an interoperability format, not copied code.

locally-uncensored: https://github.com/PurpleDoubleD/locally-uncensored (AGPL-3.0)
    Its incident-driven lifecycle safeguards informed independent watchdog,
    preflight, orphan-recovery, and retry designs. No source or UI expression
    was copied.

